  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "XtHBJh3c8H1YLClKXHJTWyxB8E0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:33:27.944Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The two stamped fields\n\nBefore a single action is signed, the light client writes two fields onto `action.context`:\n\n- **`prevOpHash`** = `hashDocumentStateForScope(document, scope)` \u2014 the hash of the state the action applies to. For a document at head that is the hash of the last operation in the scope, which the read path cannot fetch, so it is recomputed from the state instead.\n- **`prevOpIndex`** = `header.revision[scope] - 1`. Revisions count operations and indices are zero-based, so an **empty scope stamps `-1`**, which matches what the remote controller records.\n\n```typescript\nexport function stampAction(action: Action, document: PHDocument): Action {\n  const revision = document.header.revision[action.scope] ?? 0;\n  return {\n    ...action,\n    context: {\n      ...action.context,\n      prevOpHash: hashDocumentStateForScope(document, action.scope),\n      prevOpIndex: revision - 1,\n    },\n  };\n}\n```\n\n## Order is load-bearing\n\nStamping must run **before** signing, because the signer reads `context.prevOpHash` off the action as part of what it signs. Reversing the order does not fail loudly \u2014 it produces a signature over an action that lacks the fields, so the signature no longer binds the action to its position in the log.\n\nThis is the mechanism behind the hash chain: each signed action commits not just to its own payload but to the state it was written against, which is what makes the operation history tamper-evident rather than merely attributable.\n\n## The related trap\n\nThe server **does not validate `prevOpHash`**. A wrong hash is accepted and the write succeeds. Conformance therefore has to be asserted in tests; it cannot be inferred from a mutation returning successfully.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/08-ReactorBrowserClient/02-ApiReference.md, confirmed against packages/reactor-browser/src/graphql-client/signing.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:33:27.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:33:27.944Z"
    }
  },
